  "headline": "A 60 FPS presentation check closes the coverage gap Q-022e named. The build holds the cap essentially exactly at 60.012 mean FPS with a 16.6625 ms p50 against the 16.6667 ms cap period, zero steady-driving stalls, and 2.675 ms mean render GPU time inside a 16.67 ms budget. The run nonetheless records p95_frame_ms as FAILED at 16.9025 ms against the 16.67 ms limit. That is a threshold-applicability result, not a performance result: a run capped at 60 FPS has a frame period of 16.6667 ms, so its p95 cannot fall below the 16.67 ms limit and the threshold is unreachable by construction under a cap. Whether the limit should be restated for capped presentation runs is an owner decision under Q-022e; this record does not change it.",
